{"kind":"request","text":"Implement the typed definition library that the TypeScript spike validated.\n\nBuild the package that lets an author write a declared definition as typed TypeScript which compiles to exactly the data the scope pins, with a client handle typed from the definition's value. The spike is branch spike/typed-definitions-20261028, head 6fed3495fb465bdf685417f87371abf73160a358, directory spikes/typed-definitions, pushed; its REPORT.md has the measurements and limits.\n\nSource: Hugh's direction of 28 October 2026. He asked for the spike before any package, to learn whether the typed form is shorter or more expressive. Results, observed on the spike's own tests: the lending and Counter rewrites compile to the exact pinned digests (0c43dd56… and 435d9f57…) and pass the validator; nine name mistakes are compile errors that the hand-written form accepts; the typed room derives `expected` revisions from the `also` rules and runs the Nasruddin story; a due-date variant adds one slot, one effect and one timed rule and fires on the real judges. By bytes the lending rewrite is about forty percent of the original and the Counter rewrite is the same size as its helper-written original. He said to back the implementation if the results were useful; they are.\n\nWanted, with the planner free to attach to existing items and to sequence:\n1. A package (name and placement are the planner's; the spike's lib.ts is the core) with the builders: field types, slots, `item`, `open`, `transition`, `comment`, `timed`, `define`, guards and effects typed by item, `range`, `tell` and the other sends, `when`, and `compile` returning the canonical digest and the builder's findings. Shallow types only: `const` type parameters and `keyof`.\n2. Per-act methods on the real client handle, typed from the definition value as `declaredHandle` already is, with `expected` derived from the act's `also` rules and a summary read, as the spike's room.ts does over the test ledger.\n3. Derivations an interface and the MCP catalogue can share: an act's form (`formFor`), the acts available on an item in a state (`actsOn`), and the item card's slots; the lending browser model's repeated constants come from the definition instead.\n4. A typed rule-expression builder that emits the restricted JSONata profile, so field and slot names in rules are checked; until then the spike's `findings` scan of direct references.\n5. The Counter and the lending library re-expressed with the package, with their pinned digests unchanged, and their JSON kept beside the source with a CI check that regeneration reproduces the pin.\n6. Documentation in docs/write-an-application.md: the typed form as a way to write a definition; the data stays the unit of trust.\n\nRelations: the scenario harness request 736ca2bb takes the typed room as its `when` step; declared refusal names (e84e50e8) flow into the handle's types; predict (12bb1453) runs over the same handle. The kernel is unchanged; no filing-gate item is opened by this work.","body":{"conditions":"Landed on main with the package, the typed per-act methods on the client handle, the interface derivations, both applications re-expressed with unchanged pins and a CI regeneration check, and the docs; or superseded by a planner act naming the request that carries this work.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}